 ## Rules
 
-- **Slug namespace:** local slugs MUST start with `local/`. The loader refuses
-  anything else, and refuses any slug or model id that collides with a core
-  catalog row (loudly — a broken `registry.local.json` fails the launch rather
-  than silently shrinking the catalog).
+- **Provenance:** every catalog row carries a first-class `origin` field
+  (`"core"` | `"local"`, derived at load time from the layer the row was read
+  from — `promote.py` writes `local/` slugs today; the field, not the prefix, is
+  the source of truth). `c3`'s Promote scaffold still names local slugs
+  `local/<name>`, but the loader no longer keys provenance off that prefix.
+- **Collisions:** a local slug that collides with a curated slug resolves by
+  **core wins** — the curated row stays authoritative and the local row is
+  dropped (publishing later just flips `origin` local→core on the same slug, so
+  it is never a rename). A local **model id** that collides with a core model id,
+  or two local rows sharing a model id, is still refused loudly — a broken
+  `registry.local.json` fails the launch rather than silently shrinking the
+  catalog.
 - **Status:** local entries start at `"incubating"` — hidden from
   `switch.sh --list`, launched only with `--force` (see the Status enum in
   `compose_registry.py`). Promote up the enum locally as your model validates.
